 **`list.ref(x)` (`core/List/List.js`, chat-model step 2, `persistence-sync/design/fixes.md` "Adding an item that already has a parent", F7): links an item any list already holds, instead of moving it.** Same file: `{path}` (`Item.Store.address(x, x.root())`); another file: `{url: x.root().store.url, path}`. It builds that Ref and `add()`s it — so it answers the new Ref, never `x` itself. The one way to really move an item is still `item.move_to(dest)` (above).
 
+**`list.add(x)` makes that same Ref on its own (flipped 2026-11-09, the owner's sign-off, under "make the best decision… as long as it's not destructive"): when `x` is a live Item already parented to a List other than this one, `add(x)` returns `this.ref(x)` instead of re-parenting it.** `ref()` stays the explicit, equivalent call. Unchanged: an item with no parent yet, an item already in this same list, a plain object (so replay — which always hands `add()` plain JSON, never a live Item — never turns a line into a Ref), and `move_to(dest)` (it reaches `List.move` directly, never `add()`, so it still really moves). Click-through demo: [/live/demos/ref/](/live/demos/ref/) — one item in two lists, edit it in one, watch the other change.
+
